        },
        "content": "Most Tetragon events are associated with a process.\nThey're annotated with node and binary, as well as Kubernetes metadata: namespace, workload, pod.\n\nThis section shows binaries and nodes/k8s workloads with the highest event rate.\nIf you spot an outlier, you can select it in dashboard filters to see drill down by event type.\n\nNote: since events metrics can have high cardinality, Tetragon allows you to configure which metric labels are enabled (see [documentation](https://tetragon.io/docs/installation/metrics/#configure-labels-on-events-metrics)).\nIf some of the process labels are disabled, this section might show limited info.",
