        "content": "Tetragon events are typically exported as JSONs to a file.\n\nThis section provides an overview of the exported data.\nMetrics shown here are total counts for a cluster - they don't recognize all the selected filters.\n\nLarge volume of exported events might lead to high infrastructure cost and make it harder to extract valuable insights.\nCommon solutions include configuring export filters and rate limiting.\nFor guides on these refer to [Tetragon Events Export Documentation](https://docs.isovalent.com/operations-guide/tetragon/configuration/export.html).\n",
